#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# unprotect

#% text
# `unprotect(f, ...)` removes the attribute `protected` from the symbols, so their definitions may change again.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is the list of the names, as strings, of the symbols that were protected.

#% item
# The arguments are not evaluated; a list of symbols, or a string naming a symbol, also works.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
protect(p1, p2)
unprotect(p1)
#% output
#= ["p1"]

#% cell
[attributes(p1), attributes(p2)]
#% output
#= [[], [protected]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `protect`, `clear_attributes`
